  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Showers are continuing across \nNortheastern Nevada today and are expected to last through \ntomorrow afternoon. Snow is expected to mix in for the valleys by \nthis evening, with snow levels dropping to around 5000 feet \novernight. Any valley snow will be short lived, however a winter \nweather advisory is in effect for the Ruby Mountains and East \nHumboldt Range with 5 to 10 inches expected in the higher \nelevations. The low exits to the east on Tuesday, with showers \nclearing from west to east through the day and leaving dry \nconditions by nightfall. High temperatures will be in the 40s to \nmid 50s for Tuesday, warming into the 60s and 70s by Friday as a \ntransient upper high enters the area. Lows will be unseasonably\ncool the next few nights, dropping to around 20 tonight and\ntomorrow night. Vulnerable plants and plumbing should be protected\nif they haven't already been winterized. There are some early \nindications of another cold and wet system to start next week, but\ndetails are few and far between this far out.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in showers\nthrough Tuesday and in snow potential. Moderate confidence in dry\nand warming conditions after Tuesday. No changes were made to NBM\noutput.",
